From 606b4c1d1d65ce7631a60d86046ce5e0d64fd31c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:31:28 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a test that resolves the live board fails before
 touching it [daveey]

Problem: at 00:49-00:50 PST on 11-01, three cards (t_f6b0a5ea, t_13317706,
t_4d53a0f1: title "x", assignee test-worker, a "Press the pair button" ask)
were written to the MacBook's live ~/.hermes/kanban.db by a pytest run.

Why 1: the run resolved kanban_db_path() to ~/.hermes/kanban.db. Evidence: a
reproduction with the fixture's env shows the path is ~/.hermes/kanban.db
when the worker pin is inherited, and the tmp board when it is cleared.
Why 2: the board fixture set HERMES_HOME and Path.home only. HERMES_KANBAN_DB,
which the dispatcher injects into every worker, outranks both
(kanban_db._board_path). Evidence: test_kanban_ask_resolved_check.py@d046b382:31-42.
Why 3: the fixture was copied to ~/.hermes/cache/scratch/arc/probe_test.py and
run with `pytest --rootdir=. <scratch file>` (session 20261101_004634_1ec5d6).
That file is outside tests/, so tests/conftest.py never loaded: no
HERMES_KANBAN_* strip, no sandbox, no _kanban_write_guard. The worker's
descendant fence refused the first run (PermissionError at 00:49:41). The
next two runs cleared it with `env -u HERMES_DELEGATED_CHILD_CONTEXT`.
Why 4: the only kanban real-root guard lived in tests/conftest.py, so it
applied only to files under tests/. state.db has a choke point in production
code (hermes_state._ensure_test_isolation), armed by PYTEST_* env or pytest
ancestry. kanban_db_connect.connect had nothing equivalent.
Root (happened): the kanban live-board refusal lived in conftest, not at the
connect() choke point. The fixture also relied on conftest for isolation.
Root (not caught): the conftest guard denied a single root. Its test probed
the real root itself, and no test ran a kanban fixture without conftest.
Recurrence: third time. #69283 added the conftest guard, and the 10-28 hub
incident added the HERMES_KANBAN_* strip. Both were conftest-only, so this
out-of-tree path stayed open.

Countermeasures:
- symptom: the board fixture clears every HERMES_KANBAN_* variable, sets
  HERMES_KANBAN_HOME to its tmp home, and asserts that kanban_db_path() is
  inside that home before init_db. Proof: run with --noconftest and an
  inherited fake pin, the file passes 40/40 and the pin file is never
  created. The old fixture created it.
- root: hermes_state_guard.ensure_kanban_test_isolation runs at the top of
  kanban_db_connect.connect() and init_db(). In a pytest-context process it
  refuses <account root>/kanban.db and <root>/kanban/boards/<slug>/kanban.db
  before any mkdir or open. The account root comes from passwd, not $HOME.
- conftest: _kanban_write_guard now denies the captured kanban root, the
  real Hermes root (even when a pre-set HERMES_KANBAN_HOME moved the kanban
  root) and the inherited HERMES_KANBAN_DB pin file.
- detection: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_production_board_guard.py. A fake
  account root stands in for the live one, so a failing guard writes only
  to tmp. It covers connect, init_db and explicit-path refusal, a control
  board beside the live one, the incident shape replayed as an out-of-tree
  pytest file with --noconftest, and the conftest multi-root deny.
  RED: 4 failed, 1 passed (control) with the connect() calls and the
  multi-root match removed. GREEN: 5 passed.
